# skills-sync-allowlist — legitimate per-mirror skill exceptions (PROJ-039/T-034).
#
# By default every skill present in agent-tooling/skills/ (the source) must be
# byte-identical in every mirror (podzoneAgentTeam / trainingTeam / roadmapTeam).
# If a mirror MUST carry a different copy of a source skill for genuine environment
# reasons, name it here so sync-skills.sh neither overwrites it nor flags it as drift.
# This makes the exception EXPLICIT (reviewable in git) rather than silent drift —
# the failure mode that motivated T-034.
#
# Format: one `mirror-basename:skill-name` per line. `#` comments and blank lines
# are ignored. `mirror-basename` is the repo dir name, e.g.:
#
#   trainingTeam:session-end      # trainer-specific close-out flow, intentionally divergent
#
# There are currently NO exceptions: all four copies of every source skill are
# byte-identical. Add an entry only with a one-line reason for the divergence.
